## 2. Academic Hierarchy — The "Who studies what where" chain

```mermaid
graph TD
    D[🎓 Degree\ne.g. B.Tech, BCA, BBA, M.Tech] --> DEPT[📚 Department\ne.g. Computer Engineering\nbelongs to one Degree]
    D --> M[📖 Major / Specialization\ne.g. Computer Science\nrequires Degree]
    DEPT --> M
    M --> PT[📝 ProjectTitle\nsuggested titles per major]
    M --> RST[📋 MajorReportTemplate\n3-level cascade]
    
    U[🏛️ University\ne.g. GTU, GSFC Uni] --> C[🏫 College\ne.g. DAIICT\nbelongs to University]
    C --> CRT[📋 CollegeReportTemplate]
    U --> URT[📋 UniversityReportTemplate]

    style D fill:#4a90d9,color:#fff
    style DEPT fill:#7b68ee,color:#fff
    style M fill:#20b2aa,color:#fff
    style U fill:#e87c3e,color:#fff
    style C fill:#e8843e,color:#fff
```

### Key Rules:
| Entity | Required by | Optional for | Notes |
|--------|------------|--------------|-------|
| **Degree** | Major, Department | - | Top of academic hierarchy. Admin creates, no approval. |
| **Department** | - | Major | Optional intermediate. Student can create (needs approval). |
| **Major** | Report creation, User profile | - | Carries all AI config: language, content type, policy, sections. |
| **University** | College | User profile | Student can create (needs approval). |
| **College** | - | User profile | Must belong to a University. Student can create (needs approval). |

