## 3. Industry (Company) System — How it works

The `Industry` model represents the **company where the student did their internship**.

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[Admin creates Industry\nstatus=approved] --> B[Student selects from list]
    C[Student creates new Industry\nstatus=pending] --> D[Admin approves/rejects]
    D --> B
    B --> E[User.industry = selected Industry]
    E --> F{Student can customize?}
    F -->|industryProfileCustomized=True| G[Uses User's own overrides\nindustryVillageCityName\nindustryType\netc.]
    F -->|industryProfileCustomized=False| H[Uses master Industry fields]
    G --> I[Report payload sent to n8n]
    H --> I

    style A fill:#27ae60,color:#fff
    style C fill:#e67e22,color:#fff
    style D fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff
    style I fill:#2980b9,color:#fff
```

**Why the customization system exists:**  
A company like "IVInfotech" may have one master record, but 50 different students interned there in different roles. Each student can describe their specific experience of that company without corrupting the shared master record.

---

## 4. Report Section Cascade — The most complex part explained

This is the **3-level inheritance system** for defining what sections a report will have.

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start([Student creates Report]) --> Check1{MajorReportTemplate\nexists AND\nuseLevelAboveDefault=False\nAND sections not empty?}
    Check1 -->|YES| UseMajor[✅ Use Major's custom sections\nsource: 'major_custom']
    Check1 -->|NO| Check2{CollegeReportTemplate\nexists AND\nuseUniversityDefault=False\nAND sections not empty?}
    Check2 -->|YES| UseCollege[✅ Use College's custom sections\nsource: 'college_custom']
    Check2 -->|NO| Check3{UniversityReportTemplate\nexists AND sections not empty?}
    Check3 -->|YES| UseUniversity[✅ Use University's sections\nsource: 'university_default']
    Check3 -->|NO| Check4{Major has legacy\nreportSections array?}
    Check4 -->|YES| UseLegacy[✅ Use Major.reportSections\nsource: 'major_legacy']
    Check4 -->|NO| UseDefault[⚠️ Use n8n's hardcoded defaults\n7 standard sections]

    style UseMajor fill:#27ae60,color:#fff
    style UseCollege fill:#27ae60,color:#fff
    style UseUniversity fill:#27ae60,color:#fff
    style UseLegacy fill:#f39c12,color:#fff
    style UseDefault fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff
```

### What are "sections"?

Each section is: `{ key: "workDescription", title: "Work Description", description: "Detailed tasks..." }`

- `key` → becomes the dictionary key in `generatedContent` in DB, e.g. `generatedContent["workDescription"]`
- `title` → shown as section heading in PDF
- `description` → sent to AI (n8n) as guidance for what to write

### Where sections come from (priority order):

| Level | Location | Who sets it | Override? |
|-------|----------|-------------|-----------|
| **Major** | `MajorReportTemplate` collection | Admin per-major | `useLevelAboveDefault=False` to use own |
| **College** | `CollegeReportTemplate` collection | Admin per-college | `useUniversityDefault=False` to use own |
| **University** | `UniversityReportTemplate` collection | Admin per-university | Always used if no lower override |
| **Major (legacy)** | `Major.reportSections` embedded field | Admin in major edit | Old system, still works |
| **Default** | Hardcoded in n8n JavaScript | n8n workflow | Fallback only |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The `Major.reportSections` embedded field (inside the Major document itself) is the **LEGACY** system.
> The **NEW** system uses separate `MajorReportTemplate`, `CollegeReportTemplate`, `UniversityReportTemplate` collections.
> Both systems coexist. The resolver (`utils/report_sections.py`) handles both.

