## 5. Major Model Deep Dive — The Control Center of Report Generation

The `Major` document is the **most important configuration object** in the system. It controls almost everything about how a report is generated.

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph MajorDoc[Major Document]
        M1[name\ne.g. Computer Science]
        M2[degree: Degree ref]
        M3[department: Department ref\noptional]
        M4[reportLanguage\ne.g. English, Gujarati, Hindi]
        M5[reportContentType\ne.g. Text, Images, Chart]
        M6[aiPromptContext\nCustom AI instructions]
        M7[reportPolicy embedded]
        M8[reportSections\nlegacy embedded list]
    end

    subgraph PolicyDoc[ReportPolicy embedded]
        P1[strictLanguageOnly]
        P2[allowedLanguages]
        P3[generationInstruction\nCustom AI prompt addon]
        P4[uiLabels\nlabel overrides dict]
        P5[sectionTitleMap\ntitle overrides dict]
        P6[contentFeatures\nlist of features]
        P7[imagesRequired]
    end

    M7 --> PolicyDoc
```

### How Major fields affect AI generation:

| Major Field | How it's used |
|------------|---------------|
| `reportLanguage` | Tells n8n "Write in Gujarati" etc. |
| `reportContentType` | Tells n8n if tables/charts are allowed |
| `aiPromptContext` | Injected as extra context for the AI prompt |
| `reportPolicy.generationInstruction` | Overrides the default language instruction |
| `reportPolicy.strictLanguageOnly` | If true, AI must use ONLY that language |
| `reportPolicy.imagesRequired` | Enables image upload UI in student report editor |
| `reportSections` (legacy) | The list of sections to generate (fallback) |

---

## 6. Full Report Generation Flow — Step by Step

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant S as Student Browser
    participant F as Flask Backend
    participant DB as SQLite DB
    participant N8N as n8n AI Workflow
    participant AI as OpenAI GPT-4.1

    S->>F: POST /api/reports/ {major, projectTitle, workKeywords, briefDescription}
    F->>DB: Fetch Major, User, Industry docs
    F->>DB: Create Report (status='generating')
    F->>F: resolve_effective_report_sections() → pick sections from cascade
    F->>F: Build full payload (student+college+university+industry+reportConfig+sections)
    F->>N8N: POST webhook with full payload (timeout=120s)
    N8N->>N8N: Split Into Sections (one item per section)
    loop For each section
        N8N->>AI: GPT-4.1 prompt with context + section instructions
        AI-->>N8N: JSON {sectionTitle, sectionContent, uiLabels, references}
    end
    N8N->>N8N: Merge All Sections + validate + duplicate check
    N8N->>F: PUT /api/reports/{id}/generated {generatedContent, generatedTitles, ...}
    F->>DB: Save content, set status='generated'
    S->>F: GET /api/reports/{id} (polling)
    F-->>S: Report data with generatedContent
    S->>S: Show editable sections
    S->>F: PUT /api/reports/{id}/content {editedContent}
    F->>DB: Save editedContent, status='edited'
    S->>F: GET /api/reports/{id}/pdf
    F->>F: _build_pdf_sections() + render pdf_template.html
    F->>F: Playwright renders HTML → PDF bytes
    F-->>S: application/pdf download
```

### Report Status State Machine:

```
pending ──► generating ──► generated ──► edited ──► final
                      └──► error
```

