## 7. What Data Goes to n8n (The AI Payload)

When your Flask backend calls n8n, it sends this complete payload:

```json
{
  "reportId": "abc123",
  "callbackUrl": "https://yoursite.com/api/reports/abc123/generated",
  "student": { "name", "email", "rollNumber", "enrollmentNumber", "villageCityName", "district", "state" },
  "college": { "name", "villageCityName", "district", "state", "website" },
  "university": { "name", "villageCityName", "district", "state" },
  "industry": { 
    "name", "villageCityName", "website", "gstNumber",
    "industryDetails", "industryType", "industrySubType", "keyActivities",
    "supervisorName"
  },
  "academic": { "degree", "major", "university", "college" },
  "internship": {
    "projectTitle", "internshipTitle", "academicYear", "duration",
    "startDate", "endDate", "positionTitle",
    "briefDescription",    ← the key input from student
    "keySkills",
    "workKeywords",        ← selected from WorkKeyword model
    "jobProfile",
    "descriptionSource"    ← 'keywords' | 'legacy' | 'hybrid'
  },
  "reportConfig": {
    "language",            ← from Major.reportLanguage
    "contentType",         ← from Major.reportContentType
    "policy": { ... },     ← from Major.reportPolicy
    "aiContext",           ← from Major.aiPromptContext
    "sections": [          ← resolved from cascade
      { "key": "acknowledgement", "title": "Acknowledgement", "description": "..." },
      { "key": "abstract", "title": "Abstract", "description": "..." },
      ...
    ]
  }
}
```

