## 8. WorkKeyword System — How it Connects

`WorkKeyword` is a **tag/keyword library** that helps students describe their work without writing paragraphs.

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Admin creates WorkKeywords\ne.g. 'Tally entries'\n'GST filing'\n'Bank reconciliation'] --> B
    B[Admin tags each keyword with:\nindustryType: 'Finance'\njobProfile: 'Accounts Assistant'\nsortOrder: 1] --> C
    C[Student on Create Report page\nSelects their industryType\nand jobProfile first] --> D
    D[Work Keywords filter by\nindustryType+jobProfile] --> E
    E[Student picks keywords\ne.g. Tally entries, GST filing] --> F
    F{REPORT_DESCRIPTION_MODE?}
    F -->|keywords_only| G[briefDescription = comma joined keywords]
    F -->|hybrid| H[briefDescription = keywords if no text\nOR text input if provided]
    F -->|legacy| I[briefDescription = raw student text]
    G --> J[Sent to n8n as briefDescription]
    H --> J
    I --> J

    style A fill:#8e44ad,color:#fff
    style E fill:#3498db,color:#fff
    style J fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff
```

**Current problem with WorkKeyword:**  
WorkKeyword is a **flat global list** — it's NOT linked to any Major, Degree, or Department. Filtering is only by `industryType` and `jobProfile` strings. This means:
- A `Computer Science` major student might see `Tally entries` keywords (meant for Commerce students).
- The filtering is completely manual and text-based.

**Suggested improvement:** Add a `major` or `degree` ReferenceField to WorkKeyword so keywords can be scoped.

